1
00:05:12,791 --> 00:05:14,758
[ WIND BLOWING ]

2
00:05:40,352 --> 00:05:42,119
[ DOOR UNLOCKING ]

3
00:05:48,594 --> 00:05:50,816
- Sir ? - I should like to see Miss Usher .

4
00:05:52,129 --> 00:05:55,020
I 'm afraid that 's not possible , sir .

5
00:05:55,506 --> 00:05:57,516
Miss Usher is confined to her bed .

6
00:05:58,164 --> 00:05:59,678
- She is ill ? - Yes , sir .

7
00:06:00,343 --> 00:06:02,924
- Is it serious ? - Sir ?

8
00:06:03,815 --> 00:06:05,055
My name is Philip Winthrop .

9
00:06:05,859 --> 00:06:07,650
Miss Usher and I are engaged to be married .

10
00:06:09,079 --> 00:06:10,724
I cannot admit you , sir .

11
00:06:11,006 --> 00:06:11,859
You cannot ?

12
00:06:12,253 --> 00:06:15,557
- By whose order ? - Mr. Roderick , her brother .

13
00:06:15,819 --> 00:06:18,111
- He has expressly forbidden ... - Well then I should speak to him .

14
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,839
I insist you announce me .

15
00:06:22,713 --> 00:06:25,877
Yes , sir . You 're our guest . Come in .

16
00:06:36,042 --> 00:06:37,408
Your coat , sir .

17
00:06:43,923 --> 00:06:45,972
If you 'd just follow me .

18
00:06:50,185 --> 00:06:51,266
Yes ? What is it ?

19
00:06:51,910 --> 00:06:53,788
Your boots , sir .

20
00:06:55,691 --> 00:06:59,854
- What about them ? - Do you mind ... taking them off ?

21
00:07:01,494 --> 00:07:04,671
Taking them off ? What on earth for ?

22
00:07:05,610 --> 00:07:08,647
I am sure Mr. Roderick will explain it to you , sir .

23
00:07:20,569 --> 00:07:22,139
A strange request .

24
00:07:23,075 --> 00:07:24,353
This is the first time I 've ever been ...

25
00:07:54,322 --> 00:07:55,347
Sir .

26
00:07:58,692 --> 00:08:01,385
If you 'd care to put these on , sir .

27
00:08:04,624 --> 00:08:05,607
Thank you

28
00:08:14,364 --> 00:08:15,825
And if we may go now ...

29
00:08:17,323 --> 00:08:18,530
This way , sir .

30
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,846
What is the meaning of this ?

31
00:08:58,353 --> 00:09:00,349
I ... This is Mr. Winthrop , sir .

32
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,490
How dare you admit anyone into this house .

33
00:09:03,302 --> 00:09:06,185
WINTHROP : I insisted , sir . I felt I had the right .

34
00:09:07,847 --> 00:09:09,566
Well , we can 't talk out here .

35
00:09:10,673 --> 00:09:11,552
RODERICK : Please , come in .

36
00:09:21,386 --> 00:09:23,194
- I gather you know who I am . - If you 'd please ...

37
00:09:24,464 --> 00:09:27,909
[ WHISPERING ] Mr. Winthrop ... softly .

38
00:09:29,623 --> 00:09:31,652
An affliction of the hearing .

39
00:09:32,186 --> 00:09:34,579
Sound of any exaggerated degree

40
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,872
cut into my brain like knives .

41
00:09:38,435 --> 00:09:39,709
My apologies .

42
00:09:44,848 --> 00:09:47,347
I 'm afraid you are going to leave , Mr. Winthrop .

43
00:09:48,738 --> 00:09:50,309
I 've come to see Madeline .

44
00:09:50,687 --> 00:09:54,957
That is quite impossible She is confined to her bed .

45
00:09:56,085 --> 00:10:00,113
Mr. Usher , your sister and I are betrothed .

46
00:10:00,448 --> 00:10:02,728
- It was a mistake . - I don 't believe that .

47
00:10:02,978 --> 00:10:04,391
Please , don 't argue with me , sir .

48
00:10:07,093 --> 00:10:08,799
You must leave this house now .

49
00:10:10,578 --> 00:10:12,898
It is not a healthy place for you to be .

50
00:10:13,665 --> 00:10:14,370
[ LOUDLY ] Mr. Usher ...

51
00:10:18,161 --> 00:10:21,847
I have ridden all the way from Boston to see Madeline

52
00:10:22,444 --> 00:10:25,570
and I do not intend to leave without seeing her . Now , if ...

53
00:10:25,570 --> 00:10:26,904
WOMAN 'S VOICE : Philip .

54
00:10:28,559 --> 00:10:29,227
Madeline ...

55
00:10:31,902 --> 00:10:34,806
Madeline , in Heaven 's name , you must return to your bed .

56
00:10:36,477 --> 00:10:37,399
Madeline ...

57
00:10:38,723 --> 00:10:41,028
You came all the way just to see me ?

58
00:10:41,737 --> 00:10:42,988
Yes , to see you .

59
00:10:43,625 --> 00:10:44,594
Madeline , I must insist .

60
00:10:46,692 --> 00:10:49,255
- We shall talk later , Philip . - Mr. Winthrop is leaving .

61
00:10:50,508 --> 00:10:52,646
- Leaving ? - I 'm not leaving .

62
00:10:54,658 --> 00:10:56,329
He must stay , Roderick .

63
00:10:58,289 --> 00:11:00,519
Please , let him stay , Roderick .

64
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:03,897
Very well , he will stay .

65
00:11:04,315 --> 00:11:06,681
Now , for pity 's sake , return to your bed

66
00:11:43,561 --> 00:11:44,583
RODERICK : What happened ?

67
00:11:47,309 --> 00:11:49,564
I think your fireplace needs the screen .

68
00:11:50,369 --> 00:11:51,006
Does it ?

69
00:11:52,301 --> 00:11:54,154
I was just admiring this painting here .

70
00:11:54,952 --> 00:11:58,105
- Is it your own work ? - It is .

71
00:11:58,558 --> 00:12:00,878
And ... you also play this lute .

72
00:12:03,192 --> 00:12:04,278
I do .

73
00:12:07,095 --> 00:12:10,334
Mr. Winthrop , are you actually planning to marry my sister ?

74
00:12:11,999 --> 00:12:12,944
Mr. Usher

75
00:12:14,343 --> 00:12:16,622
during the time we spent together in Boston ...

76
00:12:16,805 --> 00:12:17,810
it never occurred to me ...

77
00:12:18,785 --> 00:12:20,422
And I dare say to Madeline neither

78
00:12:21,702 --> 00:12:23,836
That we were not destined to each other .

79
00:12:25,310 --> 00:12:28,891
When she left me she said to me : " I will love you forever " .

80
00:12:29,793 --> 00:12:32,754
Does it seem so incredible that I would want to marry her ?

81
00:12:33,801 --> 00:12:36,137
If you only knew how incredible .

82
00:12:37,842 --> 00:12:39,435
And I suppose this vision

83
00:12:40,868 --> 00:12:43,184
includes children ?

84
00:12:43,613 --> 00:12:44,682
God willing ...

85
00:12:44,897 --> 00:12:45,776
God willing ?

86
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:49,895
If you knew the nightmare you are picturing for me , sir ...

87
00:12:50,343 --> 00:12:51,947
- Nightmare ? - That 's what I said .

88
00:12:54,173 --> 00:12:56,333
Why shouldn 't Madeline marry and have children ?

89
00:12:58,311 --> 00:13:01,201
Because the Usher line is tainted , Mr. Winthrop .

90
00:13:01,784 --> 00:13:04,997
- Tainted , sir ? - You saw Madeline and you see me .

91
00:13:05,496 --> 00:13:07,902
We are dying , Mr. Winthrop .

92
00:13:08,627 --> 00:13:11,708
As you saw her today she is and she will remain ...

93
00:13:16,442 --> 00:13:18,797
Believe me , sir ... I bear you no malice .

94
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:21,663
Were things otherwise

95
00:13:21,961 --> 00:13:23,589
I should welcome to our family joyously .

96
00:13:24,610 --> 00:13:28,257
But under the circumstances it is quite impossible .

97
00:13:28,912 --> 00:13:30,514
But why do you assume that

98
00:13:31,058 --> 00:13:32,299
you are dying ?

99
00:13:33,528 --> 00:13:35,086
There are many reasons .

100
00:13:35,723 --> 00:13:37,228
Pray , give me one then .

101
00:13:41,804 --> 00:13:44,769
Madeline and I are like figures of fine glass .

102
00:13:45,962 --> 00:13:47,964
The slightest touch and we may shatter .

103
00:13:50,031 --> 00:13:53,621
Both of us suffer from a morbid acuteness of the senses .

104
00:13:55,121 --> 00:13:59,527
Mine is the worst , for having existed along and the both of us are inflicted with it .

105
00:14:00,479 --> 00:14:01,680
Any sort of food

106
00:14:02,499 --> 00:14:04,743
more exotic than the most pallid mashes

107
00:14:05,502 --> 00:14:07,429
unendurable to my taste buds .

108
00:14:08,179 --> 00:14:10,417
Any sort of garment other than the softest

109
00:14:10,998 --> 00:14:12,806
is agony to my flesh .

110
00:14:14,065 --> 00:14:15,977
My eyes are tormented by all ...

111
00:14:16,267 --> 00:14:17,730
but the faintest illumination .

112
00:14:19,227 --> 00:14:21,445
All these assail me constantly

113
00:14:22,874 --> 00:14:24,205
as I 've said ...

114
00:14:24,677 --> 00:14:29,081
the sounds of any degree whatsoever inspire me with terror .

115
00:14:29,481 --> 00:14:31,550
That 's why your servant asked me to remove my boots .

116
00:14:32,291 --> 00:14:35,874
Yes . And even so I could hear you coming .

117
00:14:36,748 --> 00:14:39,698
Every footstep . Every rustle of your clothes .

118
00:14:40,071 --> 00:14:42,416
I could hear your horse approaching .

119
00:14:43,276 --> 00:14:45,537
Hear the clatter of the hoofs across the courtyard .

120
00:14:45,853 --> 00:14:47,052
Your knock !

121
00:14:47,813 --> 00:14:51,531
The grating of the door bolt was like a sword struck to my ears .

122
00:14:54,901 --> 00:14:59,313
I can hear the scratch of the rat claws within the stone wall .

123
00:15:00,752 --> 00:15:04,461
Mr. Winthrop , three quarters of my family

124
00:15:04,757 --> 00:15:06,240
have fallen into madness .

125
00:15:07,158 --> 00:15:10,884
And in their madness they have acquired a superhuman strength

126
00:15:12,657 --> 00:15:15,658
so that it took the power of many to subdue them .

127
00:15:16,284 --> 00:15:17,845
Do you not exaggerate , sir .

128
00:15:18,562 --> 00:15:21,756
[ PLAYS CHORDS ]

129
00:15:21,756 --> 00:15:23,925
Perhaps there have been in your family certain

130
00:15:25,963 --> 00:15:27,856
peculiarities of temperament , but ...

131
00:15:28,187 --> 00:15:29,962
Peculiarities of temperament ?

132
00:15:32,327 --> 00:15:34,788
How diplomatically you put it !

133
00:15:36,307 --> 00:15:38,730
Peculiarities of temperament .

134
00:15:40,551 --> 00:15:42,085
[ STRUMS LUTE ]

135
00:15:45,245 --> 00:15:47,488
Would you permit me to light a candle so that ... ?

136
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:49,205
I think you had better leave , Mr. Winthrop .

137
00:15:49,856 --> 00:15:52,535
I think you need some light in this house , Mr. Usher .

138
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:15,271
Two pale drops of fire

139
00:16:16,085 --> 00:16:19,130
clattering in the vast , consuming , darkness .

140
00:16:21,782 --> 00:16:23,769
My sister and myself .

141
00:16:25,022 --> 00:16:27,347
Shortly they will burn no more .

142
00:16:29,962 --> 00:16:32,314
She cannot leave this house , Mr. Winthrop .

143
00:16:32,819 --> 00:16:35,504
Believe that or not as you will , but she cannot leave it .

144
00:16:36,726 --> 00:16:40,816
For her own sake as well as yours , will you leave now , please .

145
00:16:41,262 --> 00:16:42,691
No , I will not .

146
00:16:46,698 --> 00:16:47,569
Very well .

147
00:16:49,104 --> 00:16:51,346
Bristol will show you to a room .

148
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:58,298
I warned you , sir .

149
00:16:59,902 --> 00:17:03,039
Whatever consequences may follow your refusal to leave ,

150
00:17:04,529 --> 00:17:06,061
are upon you alone .

151
00:17:14,212 --> 00:17:16,846
[ HOUSE SHAKING ]

152
00:17:46,811 --> 00:17:49,512
[ KNOCKING ON DOOR ]

153
00:17:49,517 --> 00:17:50,280
Yes ?

154
00:17:50,972 --> 00:17:52,385
BRISTOL : Supper , Mr. Winthrop .

155
00:17:53,156 --> 00:17:55,912
- I 'll be down directly . - BRISTOL : Very good , sir .

156
00:18:06,664 --> 00:18:09,366
[ HOUSE CREAKING ]

157
00:18:55,146 --> 00:18:57,547
[ HOUSE RUMBLING ]

158
00:19:07,537 --> 00:19:09,137
- What is that noise ? - What happened ?

159
00:19:11,662 --> 00:19:13,296
- Is it Mr. Winthrop ? - Philip ! .

160
00:19:18,081 --> 00:19:20,007
- I 'm all right , Madeline . - What happened ?

161
00:19:21,177 --> 00:19:24,148
- I 'm not sure . - Philip , you 'd better leave this place .

162
00:19:24,399 --> 00:19:26,854
Please leave ! It isn 't safe for you .

163
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:28,767
Darling , I 'm all right .

164
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:38,253
I 'm not leaving you , Madeline .

165
00:19:47,871 --> 00:19:50,739
- Mr. Winthrop ? - No , thank you .

166
00:19:52,082 --> 00:19:53,129
My dear ?

167
00:19:59,066 --> 00:20:00,717
You haven 't touched the thing , Madeline .

168
00:20:01,912 --> 00:20:04,081
[ HOUSE CREAKS ]

169
00:20:06,922 --> 00:20:07,638
Don 't you think

170
00:20:09,303 --> 00:20:11,650
that crack in the wall should be repaired ?

171
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:16,980
For future generations of Ushers ?

172
00:20:17,583 --> 00:20:19,015
For Madeline 's safety .

173
00:20:22,964 --> 00:20:24,971
It was probably the trembling of the house which caused ...

174
00:20:25,345 --> 00:20:26,494
that chandelier to fall .

175
00:20:29,239 --> 00:20:30,642
Do you really think so ?

176
00:20:32,319 --> 00:20:33,774
Have you a better explanation ?

177
00:20:40,142 --> 00:20:44,567
While I was riding here , I noticed a singular lack of vegetation in the area .

178
00:20:45,824 --> 00:20:48,022
Is there something wrong with the soil ?

179
00:20:49,033 --> 00:20:52,634
The soil ? Yes , of course .

180
00:20:53,338 --> 00:20:56,536
- Roderick , please . - As you will .

181
00:21:00,118 --> 00:21:03,823
- How do things go in Boston , Philip ? - Everyone asks for you .

182
00:21:04,645 --> 00:21:05,819
Do they ?

183
00:21:06,618 --> 00:21:11,466
We miss you , Madeline . We all miss you .

184
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:19,623
[ RODERICK PLAYING LUTE ]

185
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:07,235
Remarkable . And you composed it yourself ?

186
00:22:09,884 --> 00:22:10,696
Yes .

187
00:22:11,837 --> 00:22:13,015
May we have another ?

188
00:22:14,022 --> 00:22:16,269
I 'm afraid Madeline must retire now .

189
00:22:16,842 --> 00:22:18,077
But I am not tired .

190
00:22:23,956 --> 00:22:24,872
Very well .

191
00:22:28,629 --> 00:22:29,620
Good night , brother .

192
00:22:31,314 --> 00:22:33,192
Good night , my dear .

193
00:22:39,181 --> 00:22:40,124
Good night , Philip .

194
00:22:41,195 --> 00:22:42,136
Good night .

195
00:22:47,286 --> 00:22:50,325
I suggest we retire too , Mr. Winthrop .

196
00:22:52,014 --> 00:22:53,088
Gladly .

197
00:22:54,699 --> 00:22:57,316
I trust that you will be prepared to leave tomorrow morning .

198
00:22:58,055 --> 00:23:01,042
If you wish ... But if I do

199
00:23:02,162 --> 00:23:03,501
I won 't be alone .

200
00:23:04,368 --> 00:23:05,502
I intend to see that ...

201
00:23:27,084 --> 00:23:28,084
[ MUFFLED GASP ]

202
00:23:40,423 --> 00:23:45,398
- [ WHISPERING ] Oh , Philip - Darling .

203
00:23:47,569 --> 00:23:49,353
I 'm sorry I frightened you .

204
00:23:50,538 --> 00:23:53,354
I did not want your brother to hear .

205
00:24:01,367 --> 00:24:02,470
Philip , I missed you .

206
00:24:08,483 --> 00:24:09,606
I love you .

207
00:24:10,624 --> 00:24:15,232
Madeline , I swear to you , tomorrow you leave this place with me .

208
00:24:17,048 --> 00:24:20,375
- If only I could . - You will , you will .

209
00:24:21,826 --> 00:24:23,144
You don 't understand .

210
00:24:24,308 --> 00:24:26,987
But you 've never seen the heart of this horrible house .

211
00:24:28,816 --> 00:24:32,214
Darling , once you 're with me you 'll wake up from this ... this nightmare !

212
00:24:33,016 --> 00:24:35,051
[ DOOR SLAMS ]

213
00:24:35,673 --> 00:24:36,829
Good night , sir .

214
00:24:40,515 --> 00:24:42,462
Mr. Usher , perhaps you fail to understand ...

215
00:24:43,063 --> 00:24:44,672
Good night , sir .

216
00:24:44,947 --> 00:24:46,779
You cannot order my life , Roderick .

217
00:24:47,634 --> 00:24:50,374
Is it so easy for you to forget , Madeline ?

218
00:24:50,732 --> 00:24:53,356
- My life is my own . - Is it ?

219
00:24:54,478 --> 00:24:54,688
Yes .

220
00:24:57,107 --> 00:24:58,608
- I think that ... - Is it , Madeline ?

221
00:25:00,017 --> 00:25:02,345
You hate me so much you want to keep me a prisoner here ?

222
00:25:04,813 --> 00:25:05,906
Hate you ?

223
00:25:07,648 --> 00:25:09,863
Oh , my dear , hate you ?

224
00:25:11,348 --> 00:25:14,786
Don 't you know that I love you more than anything in the world ?

225
00:25:15,681 --> 00:25:19,130
Can 't you see it 's my love for you makes me act as I do .

226
00:25:20,575 --> 00:25:22,834
You cannot leave here , Madeline .

227
00:25:23,015 --> 00:25:25,653
You know what would happen if you did , you know that .

228
00:25:26,019 --> 00:25:29,687
- I know what you 've told me . - Oh , my dear .

229
00:25:30,176 --> 00:25:33,925
Do not delude yourself , I beg of you , do not delude yourself .

230
00:25:37,007 --> 00:25:41,426
- Sir ... - I shall stay with her .

231
00:25:41,686 --> 00:25:45,671
In the name of God , would you not understand ! Leave my sister be .

232
00:25:46,579 --> 00:25:48,817
Mr. Usher , I mean to take her from this house tomorrow .

233
00:25:49,996 --> 00:25:52,660
I will not argue with you . Will you leave , please ?

234
00:25:56,647 --> 00:25:57,911
[ PHILIP ] We 'll be all right , Madeline .

235
00:26:08,378 --> 00:26:09,813
[ DOOR CLOSES ]

236
00:26:12,349 --> 00:26:14,116
[ HOUSE CREAKING ]

237
00:26:19,022 --> 00:26:21,925
[ CLANGING , RUMBLING ]

238
00:26:37,508 --> 00:26:40,343
[ DOOR HINGE CREAKING ]

239
00:26:54,523 --> 00:26:55,612
Madeline ?

240
00:27:13,511 --> 00:27:15,712
[ WIND GUSTING ]

241
00:27:22,386 --> 00:27:23,352
[ DOOR SLAMS ]

242
00:27:41,539 --> 00:27:42,972
[ CLANG ]

243
00:27:44,975 --> 00:27:46,242
[ CLANG ]

244
00:27:56,954 --> 00:27:58,821
[ CLANGING ]

245
00:28:11,869 --> 00:28:13,302
[ CLANGING ]

246
00:28:42,666 --> 00:28:44,133
[ CLANG ]

247
00:28:52,209 --> 00:28:54,611
[ CREAKING ]

248
00:29:35,719 --> 00:29:37,120
Madeline ?

249
00:30:44,523 --> 00:30:45,611
[ WHISPERING ] Don 't touch her !

250
00:30:46,718 --> 00:30:49,262
You mustn 't wake her , sir .

251
00:30:53,491 --> 00:30:56,322
The shock could be very harmful .

252
00:30:58,217 --> 00:31:02,532
- [ PHILIP ] How did she get here ? - Se walks in her sleep , sir .

253
00:31:04,668 --> 00:31:06,115
And then she comes here ?

254
00:31:07,111 --> 00:31:11,455
She is obsessed by thoughts of death . Poor child !

255
00:31:12,242 --> 00:31:13,717
How long has she been doing this ?

256
00:31:14,760 --> 00:31:17,353
Ever since her return from Boston , sir .

257
00:31:18,717 --> 00:31:20,865
I 'll just take her to her room .

258
00:31:21,394 --> 00:31:22,629
- No , I ... - No !

259
00:31:22,592 --> 00:31:23,760
NO , NO .

260
00:31:23,376 --> 00:31:25,315
You might awaken her , sir .

261
00:31:26,640 --> 00:31:27,948
Better let me .

262
00:31:30,351 --> 00:31:31,787
I 've done it before .

263
00:32:06,657 --> 00:32:09,394
- Good morning , Bristol . - Good morning , sir .

264
00:32:10,341 --> 00:32:12,177
Has Miss Madeline had her breakfast yet ?

265
00:32:12,514 --> 00:32:13,732
Oh , no , sir .

266
00:32:14,679 --> 00:32:16,705
Good , then I 'd like to take her breakfast straight to her .

267
00:32:17,042 --> 00:32:20,924
Very well , sir . Of course , she does not eat very much usually

268
00:32:22,397 --> 00:32:25,595
- Well then we will see that she does eat . - Yes , sir .

269
00:32:25,595 --> 00:32:28,472
- All right , let 's see what we have here ... bread , that 's good ...

270
00:32:28,810 --> 00:32:30,448
Milk ? A little fruit ?

271
00:32:30,693 --> 00:32:34,312
- Why , I 'll take it to her , sir . - No , I 'll do it .

272
00:32:34,312 --> 00:32:36,487
- Yes , sir . - Oh , how about some eggs ?

273
00:32:37,128 --> 00:32:40,345
No , sir . I think perhaps a little gruel .

274
00:32:40,504 --> 00:32:42,761
It 's the most she has ever eaten in the morning .

275
00:32:43,065 --> 00:32:45,265
- Gruel ? - Yes , sir .

276
00:32:47,014 --> 00:32:48,966
Oh , yes , her sense of taste .

277
00:32:50,838 --> 00:32:54,635
Well , all right then , hot gruel ... for both of us .

278
00:32:55,252 --> 00:32:56,185
Yes , sir .

279
00:33:01,734 --> 00:33:03,683
How long have you been with the Ushers , Bristol ?

280
00:33:04,491 --> 00:33:05,941
Sixty years , sir .

281
00:33:07,710 --> 00:33:11,367
- Sixty years ? - Ever since I was a boy .

282
00:33:13,403 --> 00:33:16,438
Why then this is as much your house as it is Mr. Roderick 's .

283
00:33:17,185 --> 00:33:19,071
And Miss Madeline , sir .

284
00:33:21,135 --> 00:33:22,379
Not after today .

285
00:33:23,198 --> 00:33:24,903
I 'm taking her to Boston with me .

286
00:33:26,723 --> 00:33:27,790
We 'll see .

287
00:33:38,528 --> 00:33:39,762
[ CRACKING ]

288
00:33:42,545 --> 00:33:44,212
How long has that been going on ?

289
00:33:44,935 --> 00:33:47,660
So long I 'm hardly aware of it any more .

290
00:33:47,956 --> 00:33:50,227
It 's just the settling of the house .

291
00:33:50,479 --> 00:33:53,009
That settling can cause this entire structure to collapse .

292
00:33:53,818 --> 00:33:56,019
- And that doesn 't worry you ? - Oh , no , sir .

293
00:33:56,238 --> 00:33:59,155
If the house dies , I shall die with it .

294
00:33:59,420 --> 00:34:02,285
Be careful , sir . It was about to hit you .

295
00:34:03,359 --> 00:34:04,945
It could cause a nasty burn .

296
00:34:06,111 --> 00:34:08,902
It 's that fissure that causes the entire house to shake .

297
00:34:11,100 --> 00:34:12,600
Yes , sir .

298
00:34:19,036 --> 00:34:20,236
[ KNOCK ON DOOR ]

299
00:34:23,223 --> 00:34:24,325
Who is it ?

300
00:34:30,711 --> 00:34:32,066
Your breakfast , Miss Usher .

301
00:34:32,778 --> 00:34:36,730
Hot gruel and ... hot gruel .

302
00:34:40,502 --> 00:34:43,082
It 's so dark in here I can barely see you .

303
00:34:46,476 --> 00:34:47,249
There .

304
00:34:49,007 --> 00:34:50,159
[ SIGH ] No sunlight .

305
00:34:51,637 --> 00:34:53,378
There 'll be sunlight where we leave .

306
00:34:59,667 --> 00:35:00,659
Now ... good morning .

307
00:35:04,152 --> 00:35:05,077
Good morning .

308
00:35:06,576 --> 00:35:08,415
If he comes in now don 't be afraid .

309
00:35:09,144 --> 00:35:12,472
He won 't come in . He has to take drugs to sleep

310
00:35:13,017 --> 00:35:14,080
Oh , I 'm sorry .

311
00:35:16,420 --> 00:35:17,336
Well now ...

312
00:35:19,897 --> 00:35:22,857
We 'll fill you with hot gruel and good cheer !

313
00:35:23,969 --> 00:35:25,295
You 're so sweet to me .

314
00:35:25,624 --> 00:35:27,934
Nothing too good for future Mrs. Winthrop .

315
00:35:28,659 --> 00:35:32,360
- Mrs. Winthrop ? - Open your mouth .

316
00:35:34,955 --> 00:35:36,073
I 'm not hungry .

317
00:35:36,649 --> 00:35:39,694
Madeline , I have no scrawny woman I my home , now open your mouth .

318
00:35:40,180 --> 00:35:40,889
Come on .

319
00:35:47,568 --> 00:35:49,191
Madeline , get ready to leave .

320
00:35:49,553 --> 00:35:51,434
- I want to , Philip . - Then you will .

321
00:35:53,680 --> 00:35:55,596
- I can 't . - Why ?

322
00:35:57,446 --> 00:35:59,709
Because very soon I shall be dead .

323
00:36:00,338 --> 00:36:02,490
I forbid you to say that ever again .

324
00:36:03,142 --> 00:36:05,123
- It is true , Philip . - It is not true , Madeline .

325
00:36:05,505 --> 00:36:06,818
You 're full of life .

326
00:36:08,347 --> 00:36:11,404
Look at me , Philip . Do I look full of life ?

327
00:36:14,003 --> 00:36:16,457
I remember you as you were in Boston .

328
00:36:16,795 --> 00:36:19,666
Do you remember ? You were exuberant .

329
00:36:19,992 --> 00:36:22,020
You were filled with the joy of living .

330
00:36:24,106 --> 00:36:26,906
And so you 'll be again when you leave here and become my wife .

331
00:36:28,930 --> 00:36:30,685
I wish you could understand .

332
00:36:31,127 --> 00:36:34,187
Let me understand , Madeline , let me so that I can help you .

333
00:36:37,414 --> 00:36:40,885
Perhaps you shall feel differently after you see .

334
00:36:46,583 --> 00:36:48,350
[ DOOR CREAKS OPEN ]

335
00:37:05,452 --> 00:37:08,710
- Where are we going ? - You 'll see .

336
00:37:20,566 --> 00:37:21,407
Careful , darling .

337
00:37:40,685 --> 00:37:43,296
- You don 't want to go in there . - I want you to see .

338
00:37:58,920 --> 00:38:00,169
Put your weight against it .

339
00:38:11,468 --> 00:38:13,469
[ DOOR CREAKS ]

340
00:38:18,774 --> 00:38:21,568
The all our ... Ushers .

341
00:38:32,223 --> 00:38:33,507
It 's the lack of air in here .

342
00:38:34,779 --> 00:38:36,239
It 's the air itself .

343
00:38:38,153 --> 00:38:40,505
Nothing can survive that long .

344
00:38:47,169 --> 00:38:49,222
My great-grandfather .

345
00:38:54,038 --> 00:38:55,148
His wife .

346
00:39:07,399 --> 00:39:09,052
My grandfather .

347
00:39:25,214 --> 00:39:26,520
My grandmother .

348
00:39:31,890 --> 00:39:33,169
My father .

349
00:39:38,555 --> 00:39:39,925
My mother .

350
00:39:59,068 --> 00:40:00,561
This is monstrous !

351
00:40:01,428 --> 00:40:03,714
Whose idea was this ? Your dear brother 's ?

352
00:40:04,815 --> 00:40:06,545
There is one for him too .

353
00:40:07,183 --> 00:40:08,564
Does that absolve him ?

354
00:40:11,082 --> 00:40:12,359
It waits for me .

355
00:40:13,039 --> 00:40:14,410
No , it does not .

356
00:40:17,238 --> 00:40:18,913
They all wait for me .

357
00:40:22,650 --> 00:40:24,755
Madeline , Madeline , you must stop this .

358
00:40:27,115 --> 00:40:28,942
Can 't you see what you are doing to yourself ?

359
00:40:29,943 --> 00:40:31,495
You don 't understand .

360
00:40:31,604 --> 00:40:33,992
I understand , but you must leave the dead to themselves .

361
00:40:34,926 --> 00:40:36,523
Madeline , come away with me now .

362
00:40:38,448 --> 00:40:39,715
[ SCREAMS ]

363
00:40:50,924 --> 00:40:51,891
What have you done ?

364
00:40:53,571 --> 00:40:54,562
Give her to me .

365
00:41:34,100 --> 00:41:36,624
- Thank you . See to the crypt , will you ? - Yes .

366
00:41:48,260 --> 00:41:50,494
Well , are you content now , Mr. Winthrop ?

367
00:41:52,100 --> 00:41:54,411
It is not I who forced her to live in the cemetery .

368
00:41:56,061 --> 00:41:58,165
Do you think that I wish her harm ?

369
00:41:59,425 --> 00:42:01,887
I think you still do not understand .

370
00:42:03,286 --> 00:42:05,295
And I think it 's time that you did .

371
00:42:10,647 --> 00:42:12,018
The tarn is very deep .

372
00:42:13,178 --> 00:42:15,980
One of the Usher women drowned herself in it .

373
00:42:16,391 --> 00:42:17,906
She was never found .

374
00:42:18,853 --> 00:42:22,612
I dare say it 's deep enough to swallow this house entire .

375
00:42:23,090 --> 00:42:24,668
I 'm waiting , Mr. Usher .

376
00:42:25,385 --> 00:42:28,076
Last night you asked me about the singular aridity

377
00:42:28,475 --> 00:42:31,663
of the land around this house .

378
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:38,264
Once this land was fertile , farms abounded .

379
00:42:38,591 --> 00:42:40,956
Earth yielded her riches at harvest time .

380
00:42:41,503 --> 00:42:46,577
There were trees and plant life , flowers . Fields of grain .

381
00:42:47,362 --> 00:42:49,093
There was great beauty here .

382
00:42:49,702 --> 00:42:52,994
At that time this water was clear and fresh .

383
00:42:53,920 --> 00:42:57,328
Swans glided upon its crystal surface .

384
00:42:57,844 --> 00:43:02,805
Animals came to its bank , trustingly , to drink .

385
00:43:04,954 --> 00:43:06,875
But this was long before my time .

386
00:43:09,601 --> 00:43:11,083
Why do you tell me these things ?

387
00:43:12,398 --> 00:43:16,444
And then something crept across the land and blacked it .

388
00:43:17,870 --> 00:43:20,501
The trees lost their foliage .

389
00:43:21,584 --> 00:43:24,207
The flowers languished and died .

390
00:43:25,058 --> 00:43:27,692
Shrubs grew brown and shrivelled .

391
00:43:28,829 --> 00:43:31,108
The grain fields perished .

392
00:43:32,809 --> 00:43:37,064
And the lakes and ponds became black and stagnant .

393
00:43:38,627 --> 00:43:41,729
And the land withered as before a plague .

394
00:43:43,622 --> 00:43:44,583
A plague ?

395
00:43:46,505 --> 00:43:51,488
Yes , Mr. Winthrop , a plague of evil .

396
00:43:52,193 --> 00:43:56,466
RODERICK : Anthony Usher , thief , usurer

397
00:43:58,982 --> 00:44:00,883
merchant of flesh ...

398
00:44:03,585 --> 00:44:09,796
Bernard Usher . Swindler , forger .

399
00:44:10,063 --> 00:44:13,001
Jewel thief . Drug addict .

400
00:44:16,582 --> 00:44:20,423
Francis Usher ... professional assassin .

401
00:44:24,348 --> 00:44:27,060
Vivian Usher . Blackmailer

402
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:30,708
harlot , murderess .

403
00:44:32,112 --> 00:44:34,102
She died in a madhouse .

404
00:44:36,761 --> 00:44:38,466
Captain David Usher

405
00:44:39,015 --> 00:44:43,991
smuggler , slave trader ... mass murderer .

406
00:44:45,274 --> 00:44:50,628
Mr. Usher , I don 't see that this has anything to do with Madeline and myself .

407
00:44:51,037 --> 00:44:53,289
I don 't believe in the sins of the fathers being

408
00:44:53,558 --> 00:44:54,940
visited upon the children .

409
00:44:59,985 --> 00:45:01,346
You do not , Sir ?

410
00:45:02,947 --> 00:45:05,728
The house of Usher seems to you , then , normal ?

411
00:45:07,288 --> 00:45:10,252
The house , Sir , is neither normal nor abnormal .

412
00:45:11,123 --> 00:45:13,063
It 's only a house .

413
00:45:13,307 --> 00:45:15,172
You are very wrong , Mr. Winthrop .

414
00:45:15,996 --> 00:45:19,035
This house is centuries old . It was brought here from England .

415
00:45:19,332 --> 00:45:22,672
And with it every evil rooted in its stones .

416
00:45:23,390 --> 00:45:24,730
You really believe this ?

417
00:45:27,212 --> 00:45:29,137
Evil is not just a word .

418
00:45:30,072 --> 00:45:33,096
It is reality . Like any living thing

419
00:45:33,417 --> 00:45:36,751
it can be created and was created by these people .

420
00:45:41,084 --> 00:45:42,703
The history of the Ushers

421
00:45:43,008 --> 00:45:44,953
is a history of savage degradations .

422
00:45:45,929 --> 00:45:47,946
First in England , and then in New England .

423
00:45:49,767 --> 00:45:52,004
And always in this house .

424
00:45:53,419 --> 00:45:55,328
Always in this house .

425
00:45:55,991 --> 00:45:58,939
Born of evil which feels , it is no illusion .

426
00:45:59,486 --> 00:46:02,774
For hundreds of years , foul thoughts

427
00:46:03,064 --> 00:46:05,477
and foul deeds have been committed within its walls .

428
00:46:06,382 --> 00:46:08,661
The house itself is evil now .

429
00:46:10,415 --> 00:46:13,011
No , I ... I cannot believe this .

430
00:46:13,196 --> 00:46:14,286
But you must .

431
00:46:14,925 --> 00:46:17,276
For Madeline 's sake , you must .

432
00:46:18,109 --> 00:46:20,824
Most of all , does this evil reside in her .

433
00:46:22,197 --> 00:46:24,029
And this is your dreadful secret ?

434
00:46:25,617 --> 00:46:26,724
Mr. Winthrop ...

435
00:46:28,239 --> 00:46:30,797
Do you think those coals jumping from the fire out to you

436
00:46:30,987 --> 00:46:32,311
were an accident ?

437
00:46:32,862 --> 00:46:35,866
Do you think that chandelier falling was an accident ?

438
00:46:36,647 --> 00:46:39,364
Do you think that falling casket was an accident ?

439
00:46:39,398 --> 00:46:40,782
Are you trying to tell me that the house

440
00:46:40,782 --> 00:46:43,049
made those things happen ? - Yes .

441
00:46:44,343 --> 00:46:49,799
No , Sir , that 's ridiculous , but even if it were true

442
00:46:50,355 --> 00:46:52,166
even if this house were full of evil ...

443
00:46:53,408 --> 00:46:54,908
Madeline is not .

444
00:46:55,312 --> 00:46:58,026
Not for all of your talk are you .

445
00:46:58,391 --> 00:47:01,100
You cannot take my sister out of this house .

446
00:47:02,041 --> 00:47:03,933
If she were to wed and bear children

447
00:47:04,144 --> 00:47:07,186
the Usher evil would spread and you , malignant cancer ...

448
00:47:08,114 --> 00:47:09,744
- You are mad , I will not listen to you . - She will .

449
00:47:09,900 --> 00:47:10,802
No , I will not !

450
00:47:12,351 --> 00:47:14,827
PHILIP : I 'll tell you what 's evil in this house , Sir . You !

451
00:47:15,205 --> 00:47:16,969
I will not let your sicken fancies

452
00:47:17,322 --> 00:47:19,303
destroy Madeline 's life .

453
00:47:23,673 --> 00:47:25,234
She leaves with me today .

454
00:47:32,962 --> 00:47:34,662
[ KNOCKING ]

455
00:47:35,121 --> 00:47:36,481
Who is it ?

456
00:47:38,740 --> 00:47:40,721
We 're leaving . Now .

457
00:47:42,190 --> 00:47:43,717
Madeline , you have no other choice .

458
00:47:43,923 --> 00:47:45,546
If you remain here , this house will destroy you .

459
00:47:48,394 --> 00:47:49,961
Then , you know .

460
00:47:50,752 --> 00:47:53,030
I know that your brother 's poisoned you with his absurdities .

461
00:47:53,903 --> 00:47:57,780
This entire atmosphere of sickness and disillusion is his doing .

462
00:48:01,649 --> 00:48:04,686
Oh Madeline , believe me , there 's nothing wrong with you that

463
00:48:04,909 --> 00:48:06,269
leaving this house won 't cure .

464
00:48:07,126 --> 00:48:08,490
Do you love me ?

465
00:48:12,377 --> 00:48:14,513
- You know I do . - Then leave with me now .

466
00:48:17,077 --> 00:48:18,940
I will .

467
00:48:25,848 --> 00:48:28,797
Well , pack just a few belongings . I 'll get my things ready .

468
00:48:29,339 --> 00:48:31,299
- How we go ? - You 'll ride with me .

469
00:48:32,181 --> 00:48:33,775
Later on we get coach to Boston .

470
00:48:34,875 --> 00:48:36,856
Oh , Philip , can it truly be ?

471
00:48:37,226 --> 00:48:40,487
Darling , within an hour , within an hour we 'll be away form here .

472
00:48:43,190 --> 00:48:44,907
I love you .

473
00:48:46,053 --> 00:48:47,538
I love you .

474
00:48:48,610 --> 00:48:50,746
Pack , quickly !

475
00:49:08,573 --> 00:49:12,351
MADELINE 'S VOICE : No , I will not let it happen any longer .

476
00:49:12,639 --> 00:49:14,728
Now please let me go . I don 't care what you say !

477
00:49:15,295 --> 00:49:16,551
You can 't keep me .

478
00:49:17,864 --> 00:49:21,156
And I will go .

479
00:49:21,388 --> 00:49:26,371
No , I will not let you . Please let me go .

480
00:49:27,230 --> 00:49:28,781
- I say I will ! - Madeline !

481
00:49:29,617 --> 00:49:31,961
I must leave , Roderick . Please let me .

482
00:49:32,195 --> 00:49:33,164
Madeline !

483
00:49:33,199 --> 00:49:35,104
I don 't care what you say .

484
00:49:35,516 --> 00:49:38,053
- There 's nothing you can say to me , Roderick . - Madeline , open the door .

485
00:49:38,294 --> 00:49:39,461
[ MADELINE SCREAMS ]

486
00:49:50,454 --> 00:49:52,087
What have you done to her ?

487
00:49:59,038 --> 00:50:00,233
Madeline ?

488
00:50:02,403 --> 00:50:03,721
Madeline ?

489
00:50:18,463 --> 00:50:19,850
No ...

490
00:50:23,390 --> 00:50:24,992
No ...

491
00:50:46,391 --> 00:50:48,092
Yes , she is dead .

492
00:50:48,791 --> 00:50:51,167
I told you she could never leave this house .

493
00:50:51,981 --> 00:50:54,147
- What did you do to her ? - I didn 't touch her .

494
00:50:55,122 --> 00:50:56,443
You killed her !

495
00:50:57,240 --> 00:51:01,816
There 's no mark on her . You are the one who killed her .

496
00:51:06,154 --> 00:51:09,434
I told you she was not well , and yet you persisted .

497
00:51:09,702 --> 00:51:12,416
Her heart cannot withstand the strain you put upon her .

498
00:51:18,008 --> 00:51:19,526
That 's no matter now .

499
00:51:20,869 --> 00:51:24,776
At least she has been spared the agony of trying to escape .

500
00:51:43,538 --> 00:51:45,489
One candle left to burn now

501
00:51:52,953 --> 00:51:55,632
before the darkness comes .

502
00:52:22,332 --> 00:52:23,391
At least

503
00:52:24,939 --> 00:52:28,009
she has found peace now .

504
00:52:28,645 --> 00:52:29,787
Has she ?

505
00:52:31,662 --> 00:52:33,055
Why do you say that ?

506
00:52:34,147 --> 00:52:36,261
Because I do not believe that for the Ushers

507
00:52:37,736 --> 00:52:39,731
there is peace hereafter .

508
00:52:40,049 --> 00:52:42,331
Is there no end to your horrors ?

509
00:52:45,924 --> 00:52:47,715
No , non whatever .

510
00:52:48,516 --> 00:52:50,299
For they are not mine alone .

511
00:52:50,669 --> 00:52:54,056
Mere passage from the flesh cannot undo centuries of evil .

512
00:52:55,561 --> 00:52:57,826
There can be no peace without penalty .

513
00:52:59,640 --> 00:53:01,579
Then you wanted her to die .

514
00:53:01,893 --> 00:53:03,848
- Wanted ? - Yes !

515
00:53:06,584 --> 00:53:08,371
I did not wish her death .

516
00:53:09,266 --> 00:53:11,405
I only knew it was inevitable

517
00:53:11,871 --> 00:53:13,468
as my death is inevitable .

518
00:53:14,754 --> 00:53:17,769
Our blight must be removed from this earth .

519
00:53:19,818 --> 00:53:22,882
What lies beyond is something else again .

520
00:53:38,392 --> 00:53:39,990
Must you close it now ?

521
00:53:41,127 --> 00:53:43,696
She must take her place below with the rest of the Ushers .

522
00:53:49,959 --> 00:53:51,948
One last look .

